#show: template

// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Rational Numbers]

We assume some construction of a type of rational numbers. We assume that this
type is a set with decidable equality, equipped with the usual addition and
multiplication making it a field. We denote the field of rational numbers with
$QQ$. For a sketched construction see the #local("00ET")[HoTT book, section 11.1].

Furthermore we assume that the $NN$ is a subtype of $QQ$.

Let $I$ be a finite set. Let $r : I -> QQ$ be a family of rational numbers. 
To not confuse sums of rational numbers with Sigma-types, we denote the sum of all $r(i)$ with
$plus.big_(i : I) r(i)$.

